# Code owners: a pull request needs an approving review of an owner of every file it changes
# before it can be merged into main (ruleset "main branch": one approval, code owner review, a
# new push dismisses the approval, the last push must be approved by someone else).
#
# One maintainer owns everything today. The security-relevant paths are listed on their own
# anyway, so that a second maintainer can be given the rest without also getting these.
# The last matching line wins, so the specific paths come after the catch-all.

